 "_notes": "run1 = results/revise1/grinding.json (20 repetitions x 20 deleted subjects, rng seed 1), run2 = results/revise3/grinding_cluster.json (50 repetitions x 20 subjects, rng seed 11), both re-run exactly with per-(repetition, subject) outcomes kept. Same procedure: G keys tried against the never-trained Qwen2.5-3B, the key with the largest wealth there kept, the compliant retrain audited (fixed order, default plug-in verifier, alpha = 0.05). pooled = both runs (70 repetitions x 20 subjects); cluster_subject = bootstrap over the 20 deleted subjects (revise2_analysis.cl_boot, 4,000 resamples, seed 0); ci95_iid = Clopper-Pearson, which ignores that repetitions reuse the subjects' rank tables."
